+## 10. DMA-BUF zero-copy caps advertisement (GStreamer libcamerasrc) — closed
+
+User-authored 4-patch series (01–04, DMA-BUF caps integration) found malformed on inspection: 01 (include) and 02 (`dmabuf_structure_from_format` helper) applied clean; 03 and 04 failed `git apply --check` against both the pristine tree and each other — hunks contained fabricated context splicing non-adjacent regions of the real files, not a line-offset/fuzz issue. 02's helper additionally had two live defects even where it did apply: a dead `"memory"` string field (caps features aren't fields, they're `GstCapsFeatures` attached via `gst_caps_append_structure_full`) and hardcoded `width=1,height=1`, which would have advertised DMA-BUF capability at a fixed non-matching resolution only
+Root cause of the underlying gap (unaffected by the patch defects): `GstLibcameraAllocator` (`gstlibcameraallocator.h/.cpp`) is already a `GstDmaBufAllocator` subclass — every buffer is fd-backed DMA-BUF memory unconditionally — but neither the src pad template nor `gst_libcamera_stream_formats_to_caps()` ever advertised the `memory:DMABuf` caps feature, so downstream had no way to select zero-copy import. Matches the open upstream TODO in `gstlibcamerasrc.cpp` lines 9–16 ("Add buffer importation support / Evaluate the feasibility of memory:DMAbuf support")
+Fix (consolidated single patch, supersedes 01–04, not a concatenation of them): `gst_caps_append_dmabuf_structure()` added to `gstlibcamera-utils.cpp` — duplicates whichever structure the existing plain-caps path already built (real format, real width/height, both the fixed-size loop and the `SizeRange` branch) and tags the copy with `GST_CAPS_FEATURE_MEMORY_DMABUF`; no separate/fixed-resolution code path exists. `gstlibcamerasrc.cpp` `TEMPLATE_CAPS` gained a `video/x-raw(memory:DMABuf)` alternative with no hardcoded format list — actual formats/sizes still come from `gst_libcamera_stream_formats_to_caps()` at negotiation time, same as the pre-existing unfeatured path
+Build: `emerge` completed, `media-libs/libcamera-9999 merged` (user-confirmed)
+Deploy verification: `strings libgstlibcamera.so | grep -c "memory:DMABuf"` = 2 (both pad templates); `gst-inspect-1.0 libcamerasrc` confirms `video/x-raw(memory:DMABuf)` listed as src-pad template capability
+Negotiation-level verification (not just static inspection): `GST_DEBUG=GST_CAPS:6 gst-launch-1.0 libcamerasrc ! fakesink` trace shows real per-size structures reaching actual caps negotiation — e.g. `video/x-raw(memory:DMABuf), format=(string)RGBA, width=(int)160, height=(int)120` — confirming the no-fixed-resolution design worked under a live negotiation pass, not only in source review
+Design gap identified, not yet acted on (deferred — moot until §10 next-step below is resolved): DMA-BUF-featured structures currently emit bare `format=<name>` (e.g. RGBA, NV12); at least one real consumer (`vah264enc`, see below) requires `format=DMA_DRM, drm-format=<fourcc>:<modifier>` specifically on its `memory:DMABuf` branch. Current patch's DMABuf structures would not match that branch even once the format-family issue below is resolved
+Downstream negotiation test (`libcamerasrc ! vah264enc ! fakesink`): failed with `not-negotiated (-4)` at `gst_libcamera_src_negotiate()` (confirmed against exact source line, not assumed from log text alone). Root cause isolated via `vah264enc` sink-template dump: it accepts `format=NV12` only (plain, `memory:VAMemory`, or `memory:DMABuf`+`DMA_DRM`/NV12 fourcc). libcamera's simple/softISP pipeline configured the stream as `1924x1092-ABGR8888/sRGB` — RGBA-family, not YUV. Caps-intersection failure is format-family level, pre-existing (the simple pipeline's softISP debayer output has been RGBA-family since the earlier GPU-shader work in §3/§6), independent of and not caused by this session's DMA-BUF patch — the patch only adds structures alongside the existing ones, never removes or restricts prior capability
+Side note (separate, unconfirmed root cause, not this session's focus): user cannot play local `.mp4` in Epiphany; `*vaapi*.so` not found in the GStreamer plugin tree. Likely expected, not a bug in itself — the current VA plugin ships as `libgstva.so` (what's already installed and working, per `vah264enc`/`vah264lpenc` above), not the deprecated `libgstvaapi.so`. Playback failure is more likely a missing H.264 decoder/demuxer in WebKitGTK's own pipeline, an unrelated chain from VA-API encode. Not investigated further this session
+
